{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.MassIdentityC","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.MassIdentityC","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.not_mass_is_holonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.not_mass_is_holonomy","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**And so was the corollary derived from them**, `cor:mass-identity-C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.not_categorical_equals_multiplicative_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.not_categorical_equals_multiplicative_integral","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L93-L98","doc":"**`categorical_equals_multiplicative_integral` is false as stated.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.not_nonabelian_stokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.not_nonabelian_stokes","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**`nonabelian_stokes` is false as stated.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.freeNormData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.freeNormData","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L79-L84","doc":"Three norms chosen independently; `mass_nonneg` is satisfied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.mass_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.mass_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Mass is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.categorical_mass_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.categorical_mass_norm","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The categorical mass ‖tr((λ ⊗ id) ∘ Δ ∘ γ)‖, computed via\nscalarMass from mass-identity.lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.mult_integral_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.mult_integral_norm","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The multiplicative integral value ‖MI∫_Σ (∇_A q, L ∧ F⁺)‖. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.holonomy_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.holonomy_norm","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The holonomy value ‖Hol_{∇_A}(γ; 𝔊)‖. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanMassData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanMassData","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/mass-identity-C.lean#L29-L47","doc":"**Archimedean mass corollary**: the categorical mass of a closed\ncycle γ encircling a vortex filament equals the Killing-form norm\nof the holonomy of the instanton connection around γ.\n\nm(γ) = ‖MI∫_Σ (∇_A q, L ∧ F⁺)‖ = ‖Hol_{∇_A}(γ; 𝔊)‖\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{cor:mass-identity-C}`\nRef: [yekutieli2015] ","signatureChunk":0}]}